{"abstract":[{"text":"A NFC connection to the YubiKey.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NFCSmartCardConnection","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The  NFCSmartCardConnection is short lived and should be closed as soon as the commands sent to the YubiKey have finished processing. It is up to the user of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the connection to close it when it no longer is needed. As long as the connection is open the NFC modal will cover the lower part of the iPhone screen."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In addition to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/NFCSmartCardConnection\/close(error:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" method defined in the SmartCardConnection protocol the NFCSmartCardConnection has an additional ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close(success:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method that will close the connection and set the alertMessage of the NFC alert to the provided message."}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC is only supported on iPhones from iPhone 6 and forward. It will not work on iPads since there’s no NFC chip in these devices.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC connection to a YubiKey (iOS only).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFCSmartCardConnection establishes a connection to a YubiKey via NFC. The connection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"ty